      "text": "To determine the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function by considering different cases based on the values of \\( x \\).\n\n1. **Case 1: \\( x \\geq 1 \\)**\n   In this case, both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are non-negative. Therefore, we can rewrite the function as:\n   \\[\n   G(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x + 1 - x + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   So, for \\( x \\geq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n\n2. **Case 2: \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\)**\n   In this case, \\( x+1 \\) is non-negative and \\( x-1 \\) is non-positive. Therefore, we can rewrite the function as:\n   \\[\n   G(x) = (x+1) - (-(x-1)) = x + 1 + x - 1 = 2x\n   \\]\n   So, for \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\).\n\n3. **Case 3: \\( x < -1 \\)**\n   In this case, both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are negative. Therefore, we can rewrite the function as:\n   \\[\n   G(x) = -(x+1) - (-(x-1)) = -x - 1 + x - 1 = -2\n   \\]\n   So, for \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n\nNow, we have the following information:\n- For \\( x \\geq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n- For \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\). As \\( x \\) ranges from \\(-1\\) to \\(1\\), \\( G(x) \\) ranges from \\(2(-1) = -2\\) to \\(2(1) = 2\\).\n- For \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n\nCombining these results, the range of \\( G(x) \\) is all values from \\(-2\\) to \\(2\\), inclusive. Therefore, the range of \\( G(x) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\n\\]",
